  "notes": "Hand-written 2026-09-29 by grepping every emit site (emit/_post_emit/_emit/.emit(EventTopics.X.value) of each topic under cantina_os/cantina_os/, live services only (main.py service_order). Excluded as not live: tests/, gpt_service.py, *_sdk4*/*_sdk5*, *backup*, *_BROKEN*, *v3_patch*, the flat services/music_controller_service.py (shadowed by the package), deepgram_transcription_service.py, voice_manager_service.py, web_bridge_service.py. Paths are relative to cantina_os/cantina_os/. On the wire every payload is a plain dict: BaseService.emit() calls model_dump() on any Pydantic model, and pyee passes the dict through untouched. model_dump() is NOT mode='json', so str-Enum members (ServiceStatus, LogLevel) arrive as Enum objects that are str subclasses - serialize with a default. BASE = the four fields BaseEventPayload (event_payloads.py:17) adds on dump: timestamp float (epoch s, time.time), event_id str (uuid4), conversation_id str|null, schema_version str (always '1.0'). Models from core/event_payloads.py (Show*, StageLights, ChestOverride, ChestCommand, MotionFreeze) do NOT inherit BaseEventPayload and carry no BASE fields. Fields shown with '?' may be absent from the dict; 'X|null' means the key is present but may be None.",
